WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.620
As we grow up and get older, our bodies begin
to change.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:09.750
Sometimes, those changes can be a bit uncomfortable,
or even bizarre.

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:15.410
We feel strange pains in new places, we grow
seemingly a foot in height overnight, hair

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.609
sprouts up in new places, and falls out of
other places.

00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:24.960
Whether it's puberty or just the aging process,
it seems like the human body never runs out

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.000
of ways to surprise us!

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:32.540
But those surprises are completely normal,
and to be expected as part of being alive.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:40.160
Unless you’re one particular young man whose
body changed overnight into something unrecognizable,

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.470
and entirely anomalous.

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:47.540
That’s where a very special individual we’ll
be calling Matt Terra comes in.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:53.100
Matt was an ordinary 24-year-old man, with
nothing particularly interesting about him.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.680
Sure, he was a nice guy, he was smart, he
was great at chess and video games and had

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:03.170
an impressive memory for science trivia, but
there was nothing unusual about him.

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:07.830
Every day he would get up, go to work at a
board game and comic book store, chat with

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:13.600
his coworkers and make a few sales, head home,
make dinner, relax, and go to bed ready to

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.500
do it all again the next day.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:21.850
It wasn’t a glamorous life, or that exciting,
but it was a pleasant life, and he was happy

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:23.070
to live it.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.850
One night, Matt was having a difficult time
sleeping.

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:30.750
He was tossing and turning, waking up every
few minutes to a dull aching feeling in his

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:31.750
stomach.

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:37.400
He didn’t feel feverish or sick, and the
pain wasn’t sharp or indicative of an emergency,

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.870
so he shrugged it off as indigestion and tried
to get back to sleep.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.010
We’ve all been there, right?

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:44.870
Eventually, he nodded off all the way.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:49.400
He woke the next morning, blurry-eyed and
exhausted from the rough night, but feeling

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.870
otherwise fine.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:55.120
He climbed out of bed, stretched, and headed
into the bathroom to brush his teeth.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:02:00.010
There, in the mirror, he saw something that
made him think he might still be dreaming.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:03.530
He pinched himself, and found that he was
indeed awake.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:10.069
While he was sleeping, somehow his body had
changed into something completely impossible.

00:02:10.069 --> 00:02:15.280
Where his stomach had once been, there was
a blue, green, and brown orb that reminded

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:21.650
him of a photograph he had once seen: a picture
of the Earth, taken from aboard the International

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:22.900
Space Station.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:27.130
After calling into work and explaining, in
a stammering voice, that he would not be coming

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:32.260
in that day, Matt did the only thing he could
think of: he went to the hospital.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.440
Of course, the doctors had no idea what to
do with him.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:39.850
It wasn’t like they could just take out
his appendix or give him an antibiotic, none

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:43.450
of them had ever seen anything like this before.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:48.430
Fortunately for him, one doctor knew a lot
more than he was letting on.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.610
Matt wouldn’t be the first human to develop
bizarre anomalous traits and then stagger

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.900
into a nearby hospital for treatment.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.739
That’s why the SCP Foundation has agents
embedded in major hospitals all across the

00:02:59.739 --> 00:03:03.470
world - And one such doctor was the man treating
Matt.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:06.880
On the downside, he wouldn’t be enjoying
his freedom much longer.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:11.430
On the upside, it’d cost a hell of a lot
less than a regular, uninsured hospital visit.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:16.460
So, the field agent called up his superiors,
wiped Matt’s record from the hospital, and

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:21.709
soon after, a group of Foundation agents came
to collect the confused, unfortunate host

00:03:21.709 --> 00:03:26.440
of what would soon be known as SCP-007.

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:31.980
SCP-007 is found within an abdominal cavity
on the body of Matt - also referred to as

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.900
the Subject - just below his rib cage where
his stomach would be.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.780
Most of his abdomen is completely missing,
including the muscles, skin, and organs that

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:43.910
should ordinarily be necessary for his survival.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:49.990
However, he does not appear to experience
any pain or even discomfort from his condition.

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:55.910
SCP-007 itself is a spherical planet, composed
of soil and water, none of which actually

00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:57.959
touches any part of his body.

00:03:57.959 --> 00:04:02.660
The planet resembles a miniature duplicate
of Earth, about 60 centimeters in diameter,

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.690
with its own weather patterns and gravitational
pull, neither of which appear to have any

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:12.020
effect on the Subject, nor do they seem to
be affected by his movements or behavior.

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:15.750
There are also a variety of tiny organisms
dwelling on the planet’s surface that cannot

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:17.620
be seen with the naked eye.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.389
Though it greatly resembles Earth, there are
some notable differences.

00:04:21.389 --> 00:04:25.379
Obviously, instead of floating in space and
revolving around the Sun, this planet does

00:04:25.379 --> 00:04:26.900
not appear to have an orbit.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:31.310
It is uncertain where the organisms on the
planet get their light from, though it does

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:36.009
not seem to be our Sun, since the organisms
have not shown any negative effects from the

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:41.169
lack of sunlight (and presence of artificial
light) in the Foundation Site.

00:04:41.169 --> 00:04:45.690
There are continents visible on the planet’s
surface, surrounded by its sea, but they do

00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:50.669
not resemble a continental alignment that
can be traced to any point in our Earth’s

00:04:50.669 --> 00:04:51.669
history.

00:04:51.669 --> 00:04:55.909
As for the life on the small planet - the
organisms navigating the surface of the world

00:04:55.909 --> 00:05:00.389
inside Matt’s abdomen - there are dozens
of identifiable species that bear a passing

00:05:00.389 --> 00:05:02.719
resemblance to creatures on Earth.

00:05:02.719 --> 00:05:08.159
There are blue cow-like livestock, species
of birds that appear to have scales, red and

00:05:08.159 --> 00:05:14.889
orange trees, and other plant life, and two
intelligent species that are notably and significantly

00:05:14.889 --> 00:05:18.029
humanoid in appearance and behavior.

00:05:18.029 --> 00:05:23.159
Observation of these intelligent species via
microscope and digital imaging has revealed

00:05:23.159 --> 00:05:29.150
that they operate in societies and are consistently
developing and improving their technology.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:33.930
Though their technology was incredibly rudimentary
when Matt was first brought into containment,

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:39.280
resembling early Nomadic human civilizations,
it has progressed to the level of 15th-Century

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.280
humanity.

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:45.839
The Research Team assigned to SCP-007 has
noticed the recent introduction of a version

00:05:45.839 --> 00:05:51.830
of the printing press, used to produce what
appear to be pamphlets and even entire books.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:56.439
The language these books are printed in is
unrecognizable, and so the contents of these

00:05:56.439 --> 00:06:01.479
materials are currently unknown, but the citizens
of the planet clearly have a grasp of the

00:06:01.479 --> 00:06:06.279
written word, and both the technology and
the desire to share it amongst themselves.

00:06:06.279 --> 00:06:09.319
They have also developed an agricultural system.

00:06:09.319 --> 00:06:14.009
Their farms have progressed to the point of
using new inventions such as windmills, used

00:06:14.009 --> 00:06:19.249
to mill grain, wheelbarrows used to transport
crops and other supplies, and the practice

00:06:19.249 --> 00:06:20.909
of crop rotation.

00:06:20.909 --> 00:06:25.930
Unfortunately, with these positive developments
comes the ability to escalate conflicts and

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:27.210
wage wars.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:32.560
They look to have created parachutes, gunpowder,
and other explosives, and their own versions

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.419
of the muzzle-loaded rifle.

00:06:34.419 --> 00:06:38.689
However, in spite of the ugliness of battle,
there is beauty too.

00:06:38.689 --> 00:06:42.820
The people of the planet have created new
ways to express themselves, with what can

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:48.149
only be described as new instruments, closely
resembling the piano, the mandolin, and the

00:06:48.149 --> 00:06:49.149
bagpipes.

00:06:49.149 --> 00:06:54.939
As exciting, and even moving, as it can be
to watch these tiny beings grow and change,

00:06:54.939 --> 00:06:58.689
building their own miniature society, it is
also a bit troubling.

00:06:58.689 --> 00:07:03.740
As these people continue to progress at such
a fast rate, it stands to reason that they

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:08.889
will eventually catch up to us, or even surpass
us, in terms of technology.

00:07:08.889 --> 00:07:13.510
The Research Team has not yet made any attempts
to communicate with the inhabitants of the

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:18.509
abdominal planet, concerned about influencing
the developments of its societies in any way

00:07:18.509 --> 00:07:23.740
or compromising their ability to observe them
without interfering, but they may not be able

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:26.000
to keep this up for much longer.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:30.960
What will happen if these tiny beings continue
to follow in our footsteps, and create their

00:07:30.960 --> 00:07:33.110
very own space programs?

00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:38.000
If they leave their planet’s atmosphere,
they will discover the truth: that their world

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:42.960
is buried in the abdomen of what is, to them,
a giant man.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:47.430
That reality would be enough to shatter the
sanity of many of us, and it would likely

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:49.689
cause chaos on their world.

00:07:49.689 --> 00:07:53.349
There has been a great deal of debate amongst
the Research Team about what to do if this

00:07:53.349 --> 00:07:54.550
should happen.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:58.430
Some insist that the team should continue
to passively observe until the issue comes

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:02.520
up, while others believe that they should
attempt to make contact with the inhabitants

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:06.990
of the planet, in order to soften the eventual
blow to their perceptions when they attempt

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:08.280
space exploration.

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:12.979
Currently, the debate rages on, as the Research
Team keeps an eye on the progression of the

00:08:12.979 --> 00:08:14.379
little civilizations.

00:08:14.379 --> 00:08:19.169
Hopefully, if they do eventually make contact,
they will find a way to make it clear that

00:08:19.169 --> 00:08:20.589
we come in peace.

00:08:20.589 --> 00:08:23.629
So, who is Matt Terra, the Subject?

00:08:23.629 --> 00:08:29.550
He is a highly intelligent young man, with
a shockingly casual attitude toward his body’s

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:30.550
anomalous properties.

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:35.090
When asked about the planet, he simply says,
“I just woke up one day, and there it was.

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:37.300
I don’t have any idea how it got there.”

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:41.990
Testing revealed that he is genetically human,
and there is nothing unusual or even notable

00:08:41.990 --> 00:08:43.340
about the rest of his body.

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:48.390
He provided his name willingly upon arriving
at the SCP Foundation, but no one of his name

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:53.270
and age has ever lived in his hometown area
according to public records.

00:08:53.270 --> 00:08:58.910
To verify his identity, he was able to produce
a Social Security card and a driver’s license,

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:02.210
which did not appear to be forged or altered
in any way.

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:06.550
However, when the numbers were run through
the system, there was no match.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:09.200
Officially, the man does not exist.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:13.850
It is not entirely certain where he came from,
or why there is no record of him, but one

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:18.930
researcher posited that he somehow crossed
over from a parallel dimension, or that the

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:24.300
presence of his abdominal planet added a kind
of cognitohazardous effect to him that erased

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:27.050
all perception of him from any records.

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:31.410
Whatever the case may be, wherever he came
from, he is here now.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:35.520
Because he has not yet attempted escape, or
even shown a desire to leave the Foundation

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:38.980
site, there are no strict containment procedures
in place.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:44.420
The only active containment procedures for
SCP-007 are for the Subject’s safety and

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:45.420
security.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:49.580
He lives in a sealed room filled with furniture
and other items, which are granted upon request

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.320
as long as they do not pose a security risk.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:57.170
The Subject’s room includes an easy chair,
a bed, a bean bag chair, a television with

00:09:57.170 --> 00:10:02.190
access to several movie and television streaming
services, a number of video game consoles,

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:07.780
an espresso machine, a microwave, a refrigerator,
an exercise bike, and a bookshelf filled with

00:10:07.780 --> 00:10:09.870
books and graphic novels.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:14.570
Though he does not appear to require food
or water in order to survive, he enjoys consuming

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:19.800
both food and drinks, and is especially fond
of coffee, sodas, grape juice, sour cream

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:24.940
and onion potato chips, mangoes, and the occasional
treat of Chinese takeout, an opinion which

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:27.540
he shares with the eccentric Dr. Clef.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:33.430
The head researcher assigned to SCP-007, Dr.
Cho, has a weekly game of chess with Matt,

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:38.230
during which he evaluates the Subject’s
mental health and general emotional well-being.

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:42.070
Over the course of these games, the two have
developed a friendly relationship, with each

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.290
man winning about half of the time.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:49.580
Matt asks about Dr. Cho’s family, and in
return Dr. Cho checks in about his containment

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:53.760
situation, seeing if there is anything the
Foundation can provide to make his time with

00:10:53.760 --> 00:10:55.560
them more comfortable.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:59.370
Most recently, Matt requested a computer with
an internet connection, mainly so that he

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:03.650
could play his video games in online co-op
mode, but this request was denied out of a

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:06.880
concern that it would compromise Foundation
security.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:11.030
Sympathetic to his desire for company, Dr.
Cho has begun to allow the Subject to have

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:16.680
visits with SCP-507, who will stop by his
containment facility during his inactive periods

00:11:16.680 --> 00:11:19.180
for a movie night or some video games.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:24.660
Matt has described 507 as his “best friend
aside from Dr. Cho.”

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.000
In spite of the intricate world inexplicably
floating in his body, the Subject leads a

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.840
relatively simple life.

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:33.750
He does not seem to be restless, or resentful
at all.

00:11:33.750 --> 00:11:36.230
In fact, he seems largely content.

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:40.720
Though his future is uncertain, and he is
living through a completely unprecedented

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:45.960
anomalous experience, he is probably one of
the happiest anomalies contained at the SCP

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:50.650
Foundation, and definitely one of the most
at peace with his anomalous status.

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:55.370
Whatever happens next for him, he will probably
be ready for it with a smile, and there’s

00:11:55.370 --> 00:11:57.270
something we can all learn from that.

00:11:57.270 --> 00:12:03.910
Now go check out “SCP-662 - Butler's Hand
Bell” and “SCP-507 - Reluctant Dimension

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:07.580
Hopper” for more unusual, but harmless,
humanoid SCPs!

